Studio أحيانًا يحتاج وقت أطول قبل ما يظهر أول/آخر جزء من الـresponse في الـDOM.\r\n\r\nالمشكلة الحالية:\r\nPharmacy يطبع:\r\n\r\n`Batch 1 attempt 1/3 error: Google AI Studio didn't produce a response.`\r\n\r\nلكن من المراقبة الفعلية، بعد ظهور رسالة الـtimeout دي بفترة قصيرة يبدأ response فعلًا في AI Studio، وبعدها خلال عدة ثواني إضافية يصل الرد/الـstream ويكتمل.\r\n\r\nإذن غالبًا الـtimeout الحالي في `_call_local_api()` أو في طبقة MSEMAX/Pharmacy أقصر من زمن الاستجابة الحقيقي للـlarge batches، وليس بالضرورة أن AI Studio فشل.\r\n\r\nمحتاج تعدل الـwaiting logic بالشكل التالي:\r\n\r\n1. لا تعتمد على timeout ثابت قصير للـbatchات الكبيرة.\r\n\r\n2. خلي timeout يعتمد على حجم \n<truncated 2538 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n# Continuation Summary — Pharmacy Matcher & MSEMAX AI Studio Timeout & Polling Architecture for Large Batches (75 Cases)\n\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **User's Core Problem**:\n  During processing of large batches (e.g. 75 cases per batch), Pharmacy prints:\n  `Batch 1 attempt 1/3 error: Google AI Studio didn't produce a response.`\n  However, live observation shows that right after this timeout message appears, AI Studio actually starts generating the response in the DOM, and within several more seconds the full response/stream completes.\n  The current timeout logic in MSEMAX/Pharmacy is too short and fixed, prematurely aborting requests while the model is actively thinking or about to stream.\n- **User's Requirements**:\n  1. Do NOT use a fixed short timeout for large batches.\n  2. Implement an adaptive timeout based on batch size:\n     - 1–10 cases: short\n     - 11–25 cases: longer\n     - 26–50 cases: even longer\n     - 51–75 cases: highest timeout\n  3. Clearly distinguish between 3 lifecycle states:\n     - `NO_RESPONSE_STARTED`: Generation/turn hasn't started yet.\n     - `RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS`: Model turn detected, thinking spinner/stop button active, or characters growing. **NEVER timeout or retry while progressing.**\n     - `RESPONSE_COMPLETED`: Generation stopped, text non-empty and stable for required duration.\n  4. Retry policy:\n     - If timeout occurs before any response starts (`NO_RESPONSE_STARTED`) $\\rightarrow$ retry allowed.\n     - If model turn started and text is growing $\\rightarrow$ no retry; continue polling until completion or hard ceiling.\n  5. Polling & stability waiter: Track model turn, character growth, generation completion, and text stability duration.\n  6. Detailed timing logs:\n     Log milestones: request submitted, model turn detected, first token/char, last char growth, completion, total duration, timeout used.\n     Example format: `75 cases | first token: 18.2s | completed: 42.7s | timeout: 90s`.\n  7. Safe upper bound (hard ceiling) so the program never hangs indefinitely.\n  - **Constraints**: Do NOT modify Business Rules, Prompt, or Matching Logic. Keep the 75-case batch size.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed in Previous Turn:\n1. **Diagnosis & Root Cause Analysis**:\n   - Located the exact source of `[Error: Google AI Studio did not produce a response.]` at `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py`:\n     - Line 655: Hardcoded check `if not generation_started and elapsed > 25: yield \"[Error: Google AI Studio did not respond...]\"` triggers at **25.0 seconds**!\n     - Line 649: `if generation_started and not is_running and len(current_text) == 0 and elapsed > 60.0:` triggers `[Error: Google AI Studio did not produce a response.]` if the Stop button momentarily flickers while Gemini is still in thinking mode.\n   - For 75 cases with Thinking Level = High, Gemini 3.8 Flash can take 15–35 seconds just thinking before emitting the first JSON token. The 25s timeout killed the request right before the first token arrived!\n2. **Strict Contract & Business Rules Alignment**:\n   - `src/fast_match/coordinator.py` & `dist_production/src/fast_match/coordinator.py`:\n     - Updated `SYSTEM_PROMPT` to mandate returning an item for **every single case_id** (no omission of `no_match`).\n     - Rewrote `_call_local_api()` to remove `missing_case -> no_match` silent fallback. Missing case $\\rightarrow$ raises `PROVIDER_RESPONSE_INCOMPLETE`.\n3. **Browser Automation Hardening**:\n   - Added `ignore_default_args=[\"--enable-automation\"]` to Playwright context in `app.py` to bypass Google botguard and prevent session invalidation.\n   - Enhanced `ensure_model()` and `ensure_thinking_mode()` with DOM inspection and verification flags (`model_verified`, `thinking_verified`) exposed in `/health`.\n   - Added `/debug_dom` route to `app.py` for direct DOM state auditing.\n\n### In Progress / To Complete:\n- Implement the adaptive timeout tiers, 3-state machine (`NO_RESPONSE_STARTED`, `RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS`, `RESPONSE_COMPLETED`), character growth tracking, and timing metrics in `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py` and `src/fast_match/coordinator.py`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings & Technical Decisions\n1. **The 25s Premature Abort Bug**:\n   In `MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py`, `elapsed > 25` was aborting requests before Gemini finished its internal thinking phase on large prompts.\n2. **Adaptive Timeout Specification**:\n   - 1–10 cases: `initial_start_timeout` = 45s, `first_token_timeout` = 75s, `max_total_timeout` = 120s, `stability_wait` = 3.0s\n   - 11–25 cases: `initial_start_timeout` = 60s, `first_token_timeout` = 110s, `max_total_timeout` = 180s, `stability_wait` = 3.5s\n   - 26–50 cases: `initial_start_timeout` = 80s, `first_token_timeout` = 150s, `max_total_timeout` = 240s, `stability_wait` = 4.0s\n   - 51–75+ cases: `initial_start_timeout` = 120s, `first_token_timeout` = 210s, `max_total_timeout` = 360s, `stability_wait` = 4.5s\n3. **State Machine Transitions**:\n   - Start in `NO_RESPONSE_STARTED`.\n   - Transition to `RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS` as soon as:\n     - `is_running` is true (Stop button visible, spinner, thinking block)\n     - OR a new `ms-chat-turn` is detected\n     - OR `len(current_text) > 0`\n   - In `RESPONSE_IN_PROGRES